Meowrauder — attribution and licensing notes
============================================

Fill in your name in LICENSE before publishing.

What this repository contains
-----------------------------
All source in this repository is original work, written against FeralCat's
`mk_app` ABI. Specifically:

  app/app_main.c                    the Meowrauder app
  firmware/src/system/*.{h,cpp}     four capture/TX engines
  firmware/src/ui/images/*.c        the app icon as an LVGL asset
  firmware/patches/*.patch          additions to existing FeralCat files
  sim/*                             the native-app simulator
  tools/*                           build, icon and install helpers

ESP32 Marauder
--------------
https://github.com/justcallmekoko/ESP32Marauder
MIT License, Copyright (c) 2020 Just Call Me Koko

Meowrauder follows Marauder's *function list* — what a tool of this kind should
do, and the naming of several screens ("Fox Hunt"). **No Marauder source code is
copied into this repository.** The engines here are written from scratch against
FeralCat's ABI and ESP-IDF, and share no implementation with Marauder.

Marauder is MIT licensed, so porting its code would be permissible if the
copyright notice were carried across. Should any Marauder code be vendored here
later, reproduce its MIT notice in this file and in the affected source.

Bruce (detection signatures only — no code used)
------------------------------------------------
https://github.com/BruceDevices/firmware
AGPL-3.0

`tool_detect` recognises the default SSIDs Bruce uses for its evil portal and
attack APs ("Free Wifi", "BruceAttack", "BruceBeacon"), read from its published
source to avoid guessing. **No Bruce code is copied into this repository**, and
none should be: Bruce is AGPL-3.0, and vendoring any of it would impose those
terms on this project and arguably on FeralCat. Observing what a tool
broadcasts is not derived work; copying its implementation would be.

FeralCat
--------
https://github.com/FeralDevs/FeralCat

The firmware this extends. At the time of writing FeralCat publishes **no
LICENSE file**, so its own terms are unspecified.

Two consequences:

 1. This repository deliberately does **not** vendor any FeralCat source. The
    firmware side ships as new files plus patches, to be applied to a checkout
    you obtain yourself.
 2. `firmware/patches/*.patch` contain short excerpts of FeralCat source as
    diff context, which is unavoidable in a patch. If you intend to
    redistribute anything FeralCat-derived, ask its maintainers to add a
    licence first.

`firmware/src/ui/images/ui_img_ic_meowrauder.c` includes FeralCat's `../ui.h`
and uses its LVGL image-descriptor layout; the artwork and the generated data
are original.

Fox Hunt reuses FeralCat's `TrackerFinder` class (its signal-following state
machine) by adapting WiFi targets onto its input type. That class is not copied
here — the patch calls it in place.

Flipper-IRDB (optional, not vendored)
-------------------------------------
https://github.com/logickworkshop/Flipper-IRDB

A community-maintained collection of ~8,500 Flipper-format .ir remote files.
`tools/install-ir-library.sh` copies such a library onto the SD card;
**none of it is vendored into this repository** — it is a large third-party
dataset and, at the revision inspected, carried no LICENSE file, so its terms
are unclear. Obtain it yourself and check its licensing before redistributing.

FeralCat's Infrared app reads the Flipper .ir format natively (it writes the
same `Filetype: IR signals file` header), so the files are a drop-in.

Portal templates
----------------
This repository ships **no portal pretext pages**. `evil_twin` reads whatever
HTML is placed in `/portal/<name>.html` on the card and accepts submissions on
both `/get` and `/login` by GET or POST, recording the first two non-empty form
fields whatever they are named — so templates written for other ESP32 or
Flipper portal tools work unmodified. Supplying a pretext, and confirming it is
within an engagement's scope, is the operator's responsibility.

